# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local-only files — never committed
#
# RULE: a file belongs in git only if someone who has never touched this
# machine needs it to build, run, or review the project. Agent scratch,
# personal tooling state and secrets fail that test.
#
# Every entry below states WHY, so intent is never mistaken for an oversight.
# Do not remove or add entries without asking the repository owner.
# Pre-commit guards enforce both directions — see lefthook.yml.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets: machine-local credentials, never committed ──────────────────────
# The canonical .env lives at the repo root (see AGENTS.md) and is loaded by both
# @nestjs/config and the TypeORM CLI. Only the root template is tracked; the stale
# backend/.env.example is a leftover from before the root convention and stays
# ignored to avoid two diverging templates.
.env
.env.*
!/.env.example
*.log

# ── Agent & tool state: scratch for one machine, never committed ─────────────
# NOTE: .planning/ is deliberately NOT in this list. It was fully ignored until
# 2026-10-10, when that caused the loss of ROADMAP.md, STATE.md, PROJECT.md and two
# phase records with no recovery path — a gitignored directory is unprotected, not
# merely untracked. `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd`, a fresh clone, or a new
# machine all remove it silently. The GSD planning record is project documentation
# (roadmap, decisions, plans, verification evidence) and belongs in the repo, the
# same way ADRs do. Only genuinely ephemeral session files stay ignored, below.
#
# PAM — internal tooling; self-documented as "lives entirely in .pam/".
.pam/
# Dated AI code-review reports.
.review/
# Personal scratchpad and hand-written reports.
.scribble/
# opencode agent config and its own node_modules.
.opencode/
# Generated knowledge graph.
graphify-out/
# Personal editor settings — individual taste, not project config.
.vscode/
# Parked dead code. Kept locally for reference; never shipped or built.
archive/

# ── Ephemeral GSD session state ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The only planning files that stay ignored: transient markers a single session
# writes and reads within itself. They record "where I was mid-thought", which is
# meaningless to anyone else and goes stale immediately. Everything else in
# .planning/ is a durable project artifact and is tracked.
.planning/.continue-here.md
.planning/**/.continue-here.md
.planning/HANDOFF*.md
.planning/**/*HANDOFF*.md
.planning/**/*handoff*.json

# ── Dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules

# ── Build output & caches ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist
backend/coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
# NOTE: Dockerfile is deliberately NOT ignored. Phase 1 deploys the backend to
# Render via a multi-stage Dockerfile, and the rule at the top of this file says
# a file belongs in git if a fresh clone needs it to build or run the project.
# A Dockerfile is exactly that file. Container *artefacts* stay excluded because
# `dist` and `node_modules` already cover them.
